{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/35602-lifeweb-mechanics","id":35602,"title":"Lifeweb Mechanics?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T08:46:27-08:00","id":35602,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Lifeweb Mechanics?","content":"What page are the rules for the benefits of building your Lifeweb? I know the Lifeweb has a sidebar on page 80, but it only mentioned the limitations of how many a Mummy can have in their tomb as part of their Lifeweb. It only mentions that it fives the &quot;ability to amplify the essence of the mummy\u2019s tomb&quot;, not how.<br /> <br /> Also, now that I think about it, does it mention anywhere how Mummies give relics to the judges?<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1788-haunters","name":"Haunters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T11:47:57-08:00","id":35705,"title":"","content":"The Lifeweb mechanics are pretty vague to me as well. As is I think it's very much GM-fiat, but it sort of amplifies and emanates occult energy from your tomb like unease Sybaris might or Promethean wasteland, except it doesn't have to necessarily be negative. With that being said, it might be really interesting is if the relics involved in the Lifeweb all radiate their curses on the nearby populace - but not the benefits.<br /> <br /> There's a bit somewhere in the core that says if a relic is in a tomb without being linked to the Lifeweb with an Arisen who's finished their Descent then the relic just basically vanishes. Not all Mummies might finish their Descent in their tomb, though, and that's probably how other Mummies can steal them away","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T12:59:54-08:00","id":35749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/35602-lifeweb-mechanics?p=35705#post35705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lifeweb mechanics are pretty vague to me as well. As is I think it's very much GM-fiat, but it sort of amplifies and emanates occult energy from your tomb like unease Sybaris might or Promethean wasteland, except it doesn't have to necessarily be negative. With that being said, it might be really interesting is if the relics involved in the Lifeweb all radiate their curses on the nearby populace - but not the benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds horrible! No wonder some mummies smash their tombs! Seriously though, I don't know if that is a positive thing. I had the impression than you get bonuses for gaining Pillar points or increasing the Tomb merits or something worthwhile.<br /> <br /> I feel that this Lifeweb is really a self-made cage which further binds the Arisen to the will of their masters. This is why some Mummies would destroy their own tombs, to gain their freedom in their quest for Apotheosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1788-haunters","name":"Haunters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T14:31:12-08:00","id":35811,"title":"","content":"Well, if the storyteller is using Sanctity of Merits, if you lost a relic to duat from henet, youd get back the merit points to spend on something else. This could be viewed by the arisen as the blessing of the judges, or perhaps a sudden flash of memory. It would be cheesy to make it so obvious and direct, but i would make it far less coincidental seeming than standard sanctity of merits. I would also let them get more creative about it. For example, maybe the mummy rises from his next descent with a new relic waiting in his tomb, or with visions of where to find one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T15:23:29-08:00","id":35840,"title":"","content":"Sanctity of Merits are introduced in the God-Machine Chronicles rule updates. Mummy is pre-God-Machine, so I am not assuming they are using those rules. <br /> <br /> In my games I am only requiring Merit Purchase for those items players wish to keep in their Lifeweb.<br /> <br /> What I am curious about is what &quot;ability to amplify the essence of the mummy\u2019s tomb&quot; means. It sounds like it is referring to a specific mechanic. I am wondering now if that mechanic will be introduced in a future supplement. I hope it is not referring to an omitted mechanic... :-\\","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1788-haunters","name":"Haunters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T15:18:42-08:00","id":52798,"title":"","content":"I believe it is in fact some form of omitted mechanic. It is the only way that sidebar makes sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T10:24:42-08:00","id":54744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/35602-lifeweb-mechanics?p=52798#post52798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it is in fact some form of omitted mechanic. It is the only way that sidebar makes sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that sidebar as basically saying that Mummies can arrange vessels in their Tomb to produce a Lifeweb that geomantically influences its surroundings. It's an open-ended method for them to affect the world while they sleep, promoting certain emotions and attitudes over their immediate territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:16:03-08:00","id":54813,"title":"","content":"Right, but our dilemma was that it seemed to hint at something more mechanically complex than just a vague thing that GMs sorta enact on their own","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T01:04:36-08:00","id":55316,"title":"","content":"I am still thinking that future mechanics will be available once spoilers have been revealed. I think each Relic acts as chains that bind the Mummy to their master's will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1788-haunters","name":"Haunters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T07:22:45-08:00","id":55426,"title":"","content":"I don't know about that; I think the reason they're allowed to keep the Relics that they do is for the entirely pragmatic reason that Relics are required for cults to make the Call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T13:52:14-08:00","id":55671,"title":"","content":"The reasoning behind my theory is because Heretics tend to destroy their own Tombs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1788-haunters","name":"Haunters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T15:41:44-08:00","id":55750,"title":"","content":"I had thought that Mummies kept relics to help them gain more relics. If you read the rules between awakening for a Descent and how Memory works, you can see that there are three reasons for a Descent: a Sothic turn, your cult summons you, and you must defend your tomb. The Judges (or the forces of Duat, or whatever) take a dot of Memory when a Mummy finishes a Descent <i>unless</i> it was to defend your tomb. To me, this says that the only type of awakening the Judges condone are those which are to protect their (the Judges) things.<br /> <br /> A slight caveat, which is that a Mummy will awaken solely to defend themselves if someone is trying to destroy their corpse. After the threat is dealt with, though, they return to henet immediately, without going through a Descent, so they won't lose Memory anyway. At least, that's how I read it; it could be that that refers to a tomb-defense awakening but it didn't seem it to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T17:21:57-08:00","id":55830,"title":"","content":"That reference is specifically for when someone intrudes into your tomb and then tries to destroy your body, specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T05:24:30-08:00","id":56053,"title":"","content":"Right, like I said.<br /> <br /> I suppose you can add that caveat as a fourth time of awakening","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}